Why are you yelling, Edison?

261
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:19,880
Let live, my evil queen!

262
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:24,850
Huh?

263
00:18:24,933 --> 00:18:25,817
I can't hear anything.

264
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:26,900
Did she leave us?

265
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,620
The man isn't gone!

266
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,900
I wouldn't worry.

267
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:34,137
If he had really been decapitated,
there'd be blood everywhere.

268
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:37,161
Thank you for that absolutely
terrifying analysis!

269
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:40,520
Sanji, you still alive? I'm fine.

270
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:42,517
You can just walk right through.

271
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,280
I better not break my
nose. Let me try. Huh?

272
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,290
Neat!

273
00:18:47,373 --> 00:18:49,360
Not you, too! Bye, Uffar.

274
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,260
I passed through.

275
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,580
But how?

276
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:03,400
Geez, why are you trying to confuse me?

277
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:09,720
It's totally solid when
you go through! Why?

278
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,560
How does this even work?

279
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,660
Wait, where did Lilith go?

280
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,070
Hello?

281
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:16,760
Walk straight ahead.

282
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:18,550
Who's there?

283
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,700
Oh, I'm Vegapunk Ed, at your service.

284
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:23,138
Welcome to the lab.

285
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,751
I'll guide you from here.

286
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:29,900
Keep going.

287
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:33,737
I don't think I'm ever going
to figure out this weird place.

288
00:19:33,820 --> 00:19:35,937
I'm going to hunt for
some future treasure.

289
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,608
What would that be exactly?

290
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:40,331
Like pretty, pretty flowers made of money.

291
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:43,366
Are you a little princess
or a greedy old bag?

292
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:45,400
Future Kitsch!

293
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,240
Future Bane!

294
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,035
Someone's been there.

295
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:05,660
What? Hold up! No way!

296
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:07,300
It's Jinbei!

297
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:09,880
It can't be. He's too young.

298
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,360
And he looks different somehow.

299
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,620
Okay, the first option,
this is Jinbei's child.

300
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:25,340
Hmm, second option, Jinbei
was turned into a child.

301
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,560
I don't think so.

302
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:32,960
Third option, he's a look-alike,
with wings, and a really weird vibe.

303
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:35,740
Hey, who are you?

304
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:40,500
He's big.

305
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,577
He might look like a kid, but
he's as tall as the real Jinbei.

306
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:45,860
I got a bad feeling about this.

307
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:50,200
Option four is a pacifista!

308
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:15,500
We gotta get out of here!

309
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:19,037
I knew this had to be a
government trap, I just knew it!

310
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:20,340
Jinbei, stop it!

311
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:25,820
He doesn't seem to recall
that name, or any of us.

312
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:29,591
Well, it was worth a shot, but
I guess he's not our friend.

313
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:35,877
Jinbei aside, this still feels wrong.

314
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:39,019
Sure, he's kinda big, but
he looks like a kid to me!

315
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:43,070
What?

316
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:47,780
Devil Fruit powers!

317
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:51,520
What the hell?

318
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,257
I'm ready to go, Nami.

319
00:21:54,340 --> 00:21:56,800
Are we doing this? Not yet. Hold on.

320
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:03,200
Wait, I know that power,
but how did he get it too?

321
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:20,440
Stop it! Let her go!

322
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,000
Jin... Jinbei!

323
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,360
I said let her go, you bastard!

324
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:33,040
I don't want to throw hands, but I will
mess you up, even if Vegapunk is my hero!

325
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:35,097
Death penalty it is.

326
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:40,360
Whether you're Jinbei or
not, I'm gonna make you pay!

327
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:53,080
I'll show you no mercy.

328
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:55,080
You've made an enemy of us.

329
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:57,440
Kigan de Gro!

330
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:09,900
Sea Serpent, Snap Dragon!

331
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:18,580
Space!

332
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:27,880
Robin, get back!

333
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,300
That's Fishman Karate!

334
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:37,560
Hey, special attack, green
star, skull bomb, grass.

335
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:45,757
Get it together, Usopp, you can do this.

336
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,311
He's not the real Jinbei.

337
00:23:50,180 --> 00:23:51,121
Did you get him?

338
00:23:51,340 --> 00:23:53,080
Yeah, I think he's down.

339
00:23:58,060 --> 00:23:59,040
He's gone.

340
00:23:59,260 --> 00:24:00,457
Oh, come on.

341
00:24:00,540 --> 00:24:01,900
I missed?

342
00:24:02,140 --> 00:24:03,117
How could I miss?

343
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,318
He was right there!

344
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,940
No! Stay away!

345
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:15,440
Let go of me!

346
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:18,700
I'm coming! Stay back!

347
00:24:18,840 --> 00:24:19,722
I got this one!

348
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:23,300
Usopp, stand perfectly still!

349
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:28,650
Dammit!

350
00:24:28,733 --> 00:24:29,800
Let me go!

351
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:32,200
You gotta stand still, bro!

352
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:33,614
I can't take the shot!

353
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:36,660
What is this energy he's using?

354
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:38,400
It can't be.

355
00:24:39,740 --> 00:24:40,570
Radical!

356
00:24:41,620 --> 00:24:44,320
S-Shark, dodge now! B!

357
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:57,120
He can shoot lasers?

358
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:58,897
What kind of pirate shoots lasers?

359
00:24:58,980 --> 00:25:02,392
If that had hit S-Shark, it
would have been a catastrophe.

360
00:25:04,340 --> 00:25:06,240
The Seraphim are still children.

361
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:08,737
They're not ready for laser tests yet.

362
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:10,055
Ow, what the fulcrum?

363
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:13,477
Who does that idiot think he is
shooting up our expensive stuff?

364
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:16,037
I'm gonna rip his head
off and put it in a jar.

365
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:17,296
All right, too evil.

366
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:20,048
What, you want me to
be nice to the pirates?

367
00:25:21,300 --> 00:25:23,476
Those rats are gonna die in the slab.

368
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:24,960
Way too evil.

369
00:25:25,420 --> 00:25:28,157
Come on, S-Shark, time to
beat them into the ground.

370
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:30,660
Activate murder mode! Oh, no!

371
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:31,880
No murder mode!

372
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:34,942
Trust me, I have more than
enough test data to...

373
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:36,830
Eureka!

374
00:25:36,913 --> 00:25:38,537
I just thought of a new invention!

375
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:39,855
Oh, nice work, buddy.

376
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:41,097
You go do your thing.

377
00:25:41,180 --> 00:25:42,357
I'll hold down the fort for you.

378
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,857
I'm leaving you in charge.

379
00:25:43,940 --> 00:25:45,058
The backer is safe!

380
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:46,070
What?

381
00:25:46,153 --> 00:25:46,983
All over it, pal.

382
00:25:47,100 --> 00:25:50,000
Data like this is my
morning cup of coffee.

383
00:25:54,380 --> 00:25:56,697
I must draw the blueprints post-haste.

384
00:25:56,780 --> 00:25:58,420
So much work to be done.

385
00:25:58,660 --> 00:25:59,778
Come, my sis-tubby!

386
00:26:08,280 --> 00:26:09,520
Sweet ontogenesis!

387
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:12,390
Unbelievable!

388
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:16,779
The Seraphim's attack patterns are
continuing to develop as he grows!

389
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:21,941
As I hypothesized, it seems that experiences
are stored in their bloodline elements.

390
00:26:22,100 --> 00:26:22,930
Go!

391
00:26:23,013 --> 00:26:23,940
Get those pirates out!

392
00:26:24,460 --> 00:26:25,940
Come on, S-Shark!

393
00:26:26,780 --> 00:26:28,340
Look at him go.

394
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:31,160
Oh, they evolve into war machines so fast.

395
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:35,640
Heart rate of 90, and his green
blood concentration went up.

396
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:40,620
Show them who's top of the food chain!

397
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,740
Let chum out of those chumps!

398
00:27:01,020 --> 00:27:02,300
A cursed stomach!

399
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:04,280
Why must you rumble so?

400
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:07,998
These revelations are too important.

401
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,837
I don't have time to take a lunch break.

402
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:11,920
Quick, eat something for me, York!

403
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:14,870
Yay!

404
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,900
York! Sweet nutrition!

405
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:24,177
It's sucking into my brain!

406
00:27:24,260 --> 00:27:27,140
The idea sprints first anew!

407
00:27:27,540 --> 00:27:28,800
Eat your cake!

408
00:27:30,660 --> 00:27:33,420
We brought everything
we could grab! Eat up!

409
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:39,840
Oh, come on, what am I, dieting?

410
00:27:39,940 --> 00:27:41,817
Bring more, please, and thank you!

411
00:27:41,900 --> 00:27:43,820
Oh, yes, ma 'am! Right away!

412
00:27:52,340 --> 00:27:54,060
This is life.

413
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:56,840
BMI is over 600. I'll repeat.

414
00:27:57,140 --> 00:27:57,970
BMI is over 600.

415
00:27:58,053 --> 00:27:58,883
Oh, relax.

416
00:27:58,966 --> 00:27:59,799
I was done anyway.

417
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:02,400
Keep it going, shark.

418
00:28:02,780 --> 00:28:06,440
New battle data keeps pouring
in by the second. Huh?

419
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:07,950
Oh, oh.

420
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:09,470
No.

421
00:28:09,820 --> 00:28:11,360
No, no, no, no, no.

422
00:28:15,260 --> 00:28:18,140
Oh, let's call a temporary choice!

423
00:28:19,080 --> 00:28:22,440
No, this is no time to drop an adritus!

424
00:28:23,140 --> 00:28:24,600
Come on, bells!

425
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:26,400
Can't you see I'm busy?

426
00:28:33,740 --> 00:28:34,940
Much better!

427
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:38,600
Digestion patch!

428
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,520
It's this!

429
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:44,940
Now for the experimental phase!

430
00:28:45,420 --> 00:28:48,479
Bring me all the data we
have on Devil Fruit powers.

431
00:28:48,660 --> 00:28:50,920
Bring Devil Fruit data to Pythagoras!

432
00:28:51,040 --> 00:28:53,037
Prepare for an endless experiment!

433
00:28:53,120 --> 00:28:54,355
To Situation Room 88!

434
00:28:57,060 --> 00:28:57,890
Sleepy.

435
00:29:00,340 --> 00:29:02,928
The day is an over and
York is on her board.

436
00:29:03,060 --> 00:29:04,660
Eat, go, sleep!

437
00:29:14,380 --> 00:29:16,615
Hold up, what's going on with my feet?

438
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,440
Seraphim, abort all attack operations.

439
00:29:27,620 --> 00:29:29,640
Edison, Lilith, Pythagoras.

440
00:29:29,820 --> 00:29:31,540
Your experiment is over.

441
00:29:31,860 --> 00:29:33,820
Oh, there goes my name.

442
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,230
No!

443
00:29:36,180 --> 00:29:38,880
It's more just kidding, it's a good part.

444
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:40,520
Stupid Killjoy!

445
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:42,230
Eureka!

446
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:54,077
I don't know what happened, but
I think that guy just saved us.

447
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:56,457
Whoever he is, I don't trust him one bit.

448
00:29:56,540 --> 00:29:59,840
He must be the guy Lilith
was talking to. No way!

449
00:30:00,100 --> 00:30:00,960
Could he be?

450
00:30:01,500 --> 00:30:02,500
I am Dr.

451
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:04,540
Vegapunk, Shaka the Good.

452
00:30:09,220 --> 00:30:10,260
Another Vegapunk?

453
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:12,437
Not overdoing it, don't you think?

454
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:16,160
So, you are the famous Straw
Hat Crew. Yeah, pleasure.

455
00:30:16,420 --> 00:30:19,337
Now can you tell us why our
shoes are stuck to the floor?

456
00:30:19,420 --> 00:30:21,100
Dom's shoes are magnetized.

457
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:23,737
We can control them
remotely inside the lab.

458
00:30:23,820 --> 00:30:25,760
Resistance is futile, I take it.

459
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:28,440
I cannot trust pirates.

460
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:31,260
Okay, but are you really Dr. Vegapunk?

461
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:33,877
Because you're like the
third one we met today.

462
00:30:33,960 --> 00:30:34,790
Indeed.

463
00:30:34,873 --> 00:30:36,620
We are all Vegapunk.

464
00:30:36,920 --> 00:30:37,917
What does that mean?

465
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:40,040
How many Vegapunks are there?

466
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:42,860
Am I Vegapunk? What?

467
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:45,500
No, bro, will you stop embarrassing me?

468
00:30:50,260 --> 00:30:54,140
Tell me, does this island
look like the future to you?

469
00:30:54,720 --> 00:30:55,550
What?

470
00:30:55,633 --> 00:30:56,618
Are you kidding me?

471
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,200
Of course it does!

472
00:30:58,580 --> 00:31:00,977
You got mechanical
monsters out at the sea.

473
00:31:01,060 --> 00:31:02,707
Vegaforce One flying around.

474
00:31:02,860 --> 00:31:04,917
Air and temperature
regulations everywhere.

475
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,777
this place looks like the super future!

476
00:31:06,860 --> 00:31:09,919
The city here is like nothing
I've ever seen before.

477
00:31:10,040 --> 00:31:12,797
I want to check out that
tech from top to bottom.

478
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,697
This island's the freaking ball.

479
00:31:14,780 --> 00:31:16,660
So don't be a hater, Vangapro.

480
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:19,160
Let us go explore it. Pretty please.

481
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:22,555
It will never surpass its predecessor.

482
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:27,260
This island is the past.

483
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:31,904
How could you call it the past?

484
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:38,717
Hypothetically speaking, if I told
you there was an advanced kingdom,

485
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:43,900
much like this island, that existed
900 years ago, would you believe me?

486
00:31:44,740 --> 00:31:46,620
Wait, like 9-0-0?

487
00:31:46,940 --> 00:31:48,400
That's crazy talk, bro!

488
00:31:54,340 --> 00:31:55,380
Chopper, look!

489
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:58,180
It's really real, it's not a hop of it!

490
00:31:58,400 --> 00:31:59,777
Gotta come check this out!

491
00:31:59,860 --> 00:32:00,980
See that?

492
00:32:01,180 --> 00:32:02,040
It's metal!

493
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:08,080
Looks impressive, but it's pretty beat up.

494
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:11,617
Do you think this thing
used to move around?

495
00:32:11,700 --> 00:32:14,797
Well, that would be a stretch,
even with this Isla's tech.

496
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,586
It looks like it's quite old.

497
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:20,280
Can we ride it? Yeah! Great idea!

498
00:32:20,660 --> 00:32:21,954
I'll reach into the...

499
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:40,000
Thank you.
